    "draft": false,
    "body": "## Why\nNativeWeave now has one product: strongly typed C# Fluent ORM over PostgreSQL and SQLite, using Rust SeaQuery and SQLx with Native AOT. The prior Perf-01 work has stopped. Plan PR IzuSharp/Plan#24 established this scope before this design change.\n\n## Changes\n- Retain Database Host, provider independence, pools, sessions, transactions, migrations, binding, static models/DTOs, relations/CRUD, streams and lifecycle/AOT requirements.\n- Remove NativeWeave server/protocol/compression/demo products from current requirements, architecture, API and packaging guidance. Applications choose their own standard host.\n- Preserve historical acceptance, prototypes, registries and original specifications byte for byte; keep frozen historical gates and add current scope validation.\n- Define the twelve database candidate packages and four Linux x64 PostgreSQL/SQLite JIT/AOT consumer cells.\n\n## Validation\nThe exact published head `3d1b4d5d80b8e3d8790481276a8333c0d2a25754` (tree `74f886a74a38d0478d1c4b4a22ea17383dfd0424`) passed current scope/API CI [44906037807](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave-Design/actions/runs/44906037807), frozen historical CI [44906037741](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave-Design/actions/runs/44906037741), and push scope CI [44906028381](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave-Design/actions/runs/44906028381). The current validator covers 22 active documents, 24 exact archive identities, the twelve-package closure and eight rejection controls.\n\nIndependent technical review by `/root/old_task_inventory` confirmed the exact tree and resolved the static generator ownership finding. This is an agent technical review, not a second GitHub account approval. It claims no product runtime acceptance. Product regression and outside-source package acceptance remain in progress in IzuSharp/Plan#24; merge and main-CI closeout follow those results.\n\nNo performance work or new server wrapper is included.",
    "title": "DB-Scope-01: narrow the current design to the database product",
